The code snippet provided is from a C++ implementation where a process handle is opened but not closed. This can lead to resource leaks, which might cause the program to consume more memory than necessary and eventually crash due to insufficient resources. To fix this issue, ensure that the process handle is properly closed after it is no longer needed. Here's how you can modify the code:

```cpp
void PluginChannel::OnChannelConnected(int32 peer_pid) {
  base::ProcessHandle handle;
  if (!base::OpenProcessHandle(peer_pid, &handle)) {
    NOTREACHED();
  }
  renderer_handle_ = handle;
  NPChannelBase::OnChannelConnected(peer_pid);

  // Close the process handle when done
  base::CloseProcessHandle(handle);
}
```

This modification ensures that the process handle is closed after it has been used, preventing resource leaks and improving the overall stability of the program.

